WHY SHARE-ALIKE, WHEN OTHER JETBRAINS ACADEMY COURSES ARE MIT

This is a deliberate choice, not an oversight, and it should not be "corrected"
to match the other courses.

AdaCore's repository carries a CC BY 4.0 LICENSE file, but the course content
itself states, in its own front matter, that it is published under CC BY-SA and
that "if you remix, transform, or build upon the material, you must distribute
your contributions under the same license as the original". The same wording
appears in other AdaCore courses, so it is not a slip. Where two statements about
the same work conflict, this adaptation follows the more specific and more
restrictive one.

The consequence is that this course cannot be relicensed MIT, which is what the
JetBrains Marketplace uses for its own courses. If AdaCore ever reconciles the
two statements in favour of CC BY 4.0, this can be revisited.

The Ada source code written specifically for this course -- the Ada_Check test
harness under harness/, and the tests under each task's tests/ directory -- is
original work and is offered under the same licence for simplicity.
